|~ `::doc`, the kind of a doc, its constructor and its refusals, and
   the verbs of docs. Each resides on `::qlang/doc`, the kind whose
   module declares it, and reads the doc's shape for the query. ~|

::doc
  |~~ The kind of a doc, prose as a value, the value of a doc literal:
      text that carries quotes of qlang. It is how the language says what
      it is: every page is a doc, `doc` answers the page of a name, and
      because a doc is a value its code is checked and the next step can
      take it apart. A quote with no tag is a law of the page, which
      `runLaws` holds to answer true; a quote under `::link` is a
      link, a query a reader follows. `content` answers its text,
      `segments` its parts, `laws` its laws, `links` its links and
      `snippets` its snippets.
      ::snippet~(::doc | spec | /verbs) lists its verbs. ::link~(::link | doc)
      ::link~(::qlang | doc :hypertext)

      ~(::number/add | doc | type | eq ::doc)
      ~(|~~ a ~(add 1) b ~~| | segments | count | eq 3)
      ~(["a" ~(add 1)] | tag ::doc | eq (|~~a~(add 1)~~|))
  ~~|
  ::builtin{:impl :qlang/type/doc}

::DocPayloadNotVecError
  |~~ `::doc` payload must be a Vec of segments.

      ~(
        ::doc"x"
        !| [type /actualType]
        |  eq [::DocPayloadNotVecError ::string]
       )
  ~~|

::DocElementNotSegmentError
  |~~ Every element of a doc is a segment, a string of prose or a
      quote, and another value is refused at the index it stands at.

      ~(
        ["a" 1] | tag ::doc
        !| [type /index]
        |  eq [::DocElementNotSegmentError 1]
       )
  ~~|

:content
  |~~ The text of the doc: its prose with each quote written where it
      stands.

      ~(|~~ a ~(add 1) b ~~| | content | eq " a ~(add 1) b ")
      ~(::vec/join | doc | content | contains "separator")
  ~~|
  ::verb~(:returns ::string | ::builtin{:impl :qlang/prim/docContent})

:segments
  |~~ The parts of the doc in their order: each run of prose a string
      and each span that reads as code a quote, bare or under the tags
      of its role.

      ~(|~~ a ~(add 1) b ~~| | segments | eq [" a " ~(add 1) " b "])
      ~(|~~ see ~(add 1) ~~| | segments | count | eq 3)
  ~~|
  ::verb~(:returns ::vec | ::builtin{:impl :qlang/prim/docSegments})

:laws
  |~~ The laws of the doc in their order: each quote with no tag, which
      `runLaws` holds to answer true; a quote under a tag, a link or a
      snippet, is no law.

      ~(|~~ a ~(add 1) b ~(mul 2) ~~| | laws | eq [~(add 1) ~(mul 2)])
      ~("x" | add 1 !| explain | page | laws | count | eq 1)
  ~~|
  ::verb~(:returns ::vec | ::builtin{:impl :qlang/prim/docLaws})

:links
  |~~ The links of the doc in their order: each quote under a stack of
      tags that holds `::link`, a query a reader follows.

      ~(|~~ see ::link~(::qlang | manifest) ~~| | links | count | eq 1)
      ~(|~~ ::link~(::qlang | manifest) ~~| | links | first | :l / | null | apply l | has ::number)
  ~~|
  ::verb~(:returns ::vec | ::builtin{:impl :qlang/prim/docLinks})

:snippets
  |~~ The snippets of the doc in their order: each quote under a stack
      of tags that holds `::snippet`, a query a reader runs to see what
      it shows.

      ~(|~~ run ::snippet~([2 1] | sort) ~~| | snippets | count | eq 1)
      ~(|~~ ::snippet~([2 1] | sort) ~~| | snippets * open | eq [[1 2]])
  ~~|
  ::verb~(:returns ::vec | ::builtin{:impl :qlang/prim/docSnippets})
